# AI Platform Legal Analysis
#Data Retention
OpenAI (ChatGPT Enterprise): Does not use customer Inputs or Outputs to train OpenAI models. Retention is maintained only to provide the services and comply with legal requirements.
Anthrophic (Claude/Bedrock): Data retention policies differ per tier, but Enterprise tiers default to zero model training on your data.
Google (Vertex/Gemini):  Google’s Gemini API Additional Terms of Service state that your Customer Data is not used to train any Google or third-party foundation models. Data is retained strictly to provide the service.

#Intellectual Property Ownership of Inputs & Outputs
OpenAI: Assigns all rights to the Output to the user, provided the user complies with the terms. Does not claim ownership of user Inputs.
Microsoft (Copilot/Azure): Generally does not claim ownership of the user's inputs or outputs. Provides varying levels of copyright protection for rights of enterprise customers who face claims of intellectual property infringement. 
Google: Explicitly clarifies that it does not claim ownership between user's inputs and outputs. 

#Privacy Boundaries
Microsoft: Operates under the Microsoft Services Agreement, outlining standard privacy controls. Enterprise accounts are secured by HIPAA and GDPR compliance commitments, protecting against unauthorized internal use or vendor access.

